// Five Realms Plugin -- Lists panel
//
// Phase 1 of an MTG-compatible rules engine: state model, zones, game objects, turn
// structure, priority, mana, deterministic RNG, and a single applyAction reducer. Card
// data, type grammar, and mana-cost grammar are fixed by
// docs/specs/2026-08-21-five-realms-card-model.md -- conformed to exactly. Stack
// resolution/targeting, combat damage assignment, state-based actions, layers, replacement
// effects, and keyword abilities are implemented; only expansion beyond the fixture cards is
// a later phase.
//
// All top-level names are prefixed `fr` so they cannot collide with a consuming
// generator's own names once imported. One import of our own: simpleGenFooter, the
// standard Perchance footer (rathji-plugin-template's convention), used only by this
// docs page. See NOTES.md for a citation on every non-obvious DSL construct used below;
// the engine logic itself is our own composition and is not DSL, so it carries no
// citation.
//
// $output (the plugin's public API) is the 13-op entry point at the bottom of this file.


// =====================================================================
// FEATURE TODO (all of #2..#6 implemented; this list is now complete)
// =====================================================================
//
// #2 (multi-color mana abilities / dual lands) is implemented: frActionActivateAbility
// validates a chosenColor on multi-color producers and adds 1 mana of that color, the
// dual-land fixture luminous-lagoon ("WU") and the {C} producer prismatic-core are in
// frCardDb, and frLegalActions offers one action per produced color. #3 (multiple
// targets & modal "Choose one" spells) is implemented too: card records declare
// targeting ({ min, max, distinct, slots }) and/or a modes: [...] list, frActionCastSpell
// validates the chosen mode and the full target-set, frLegalActions enumerates every
// legal ordered target-set per mode, and resolution reads targets/mode off the stack
// entry. The rest of this list is not implemented; it is tracked here so the work is
// not lost. For reference, it deliberately excludes what already exists: combat basics
// (attackers/blockers/evasion/first-strike/trample-to-player), the keyword library
// (flying, trample, haste, vigilance, defender, reach, menace, deathtouch, double
// strike, lifelink, hexproof, indestructible, skulk, ward), triggers on enter/attack/
// combat-damage, aura attach + buffs, +1/+1 counters, effect layers with timestamps,
// single-target legality, sorcery/instant timing, the SBA loop (0-toughness, lethal,
// Aura, life<=0), and seeded RNG/snapshot.
//
// #4 (data-driven card effects) is implemented: card records now declare
// effects/triggers/abilities/auraBuff instead of id-matching. The effect-template
// library in frApplyOneEffect covers damage / damageAll / life / draw / discard /
// destroy / pump (+N/+N until EoT) / shield / scry / addMana / token / counter /
// tutor slots, with X and chosen targets/mode substituted at resolution. Generic
// activated abilities carry arbitrary costs ({T}, mana, sacrifice self, life), and
// data-driven triggers fire on enter / attack / combat-damage-to-player. Fixture
// cards: verdant-surge, ember-conflagration, verdant-call (tokens), ember-hound
// ({1},{T} pings), faceted-ember-core (combust), tide-banishment (counter), and
// the trigger suite on sunward-sentinel / nautilus-seer / bramble-warden /
// thornshroud-stalker. #5 (combat damage assignment order) is implemented, see
// below. The rest of this list is not implemented yet; it is tracked here so the
// work is not lost.
//
// #5 (combat damage assignment order / double blockers) is implemented:
// frActionDeclareBlockers now rejects a blocker assigned to two attackers, accepts
// an optional 1-based order per multi-blocked attacker (either every blocker of an
// attacker declares an order, or none, and declared orders must be a permutation of
// 1..n), and normalizes state.combatBlocks into { attacker, blocker, order } sorted
// by order (insertion order when none declared); frLegalActions enumerates every
// blocker order permutation (capped at 4096 actions) and the order is what the
// blocking player picks at declare-blockers time. A pre-existing bug is fixed too:
// declareBlockers checked the attacker's tapped status, so a tapped attacker could
// never be blocked. frDoCombatDamage assigns the attacker's power across its
// blockers in declared order -- lethal to the first blocker, the remainder onward,
// the last blocker absorbing whatever is left unless trample spills past it to the
// player -- with damage within a wave simultaneous (SBA runs between waves), and
// trample spill now travels the full combat-damage path (shields, lifelink,
// triggers) instead of bypassing it. Fixture test: a 5-power attacker double-blocked
// by two 3-toughness creatures dies to the first only when order says so. #6 (custom
// card database injection) is implemented, see below.
//
// #6 (custom card database injection + null-safe lookups) is implemented: frGameNew
// accepts config.cards (a \{id: card\} map merged over frCardDb -- fixture entries stay,
// custom entries win on a shared id) and publishes the merged database as
// window.FIVE_REALMS_CARDDB, which frCardGet, $output("cards") and frGameDefaultDeck
// resolve against until the next newGame (a newGame without config.cards restores the
// fixture DB -- the same lazy window-global idiom as the art payload). Every frCardGet
// consumer now null-checks: frCheckStateBasedActions and frResolveSpell skip unknown
// cards (their subtypes reads are guarded too), and frActionDeclareAttackers rejects
// one with a clean lastActionError -- a card id outside any DB no longer crashes the
// reducer/SBA. Fixture test: newGame with a tiny custom DB of non-fixture cards plays
// a full turn (land, tap, cast, combat, SBA) with zero errors, and a bogus id is
// skipped, not thrown on. The TODO list is complete.

$meta
  title = Five Realms Plugin
  description = An MTG-compatible rules engine, a 47-card data-driven database, and a 52-asset inline-SVG card renderer, behind one 13-op $output. Zones, turn structure, priority, mana, seeded shuffling, an action reducer, stack resolution with multi-target and modal spells, data-driven card effects (templates, triggers, generic activated abilities), plus the full state-based-actions loop, layered continuous effects, a keyword-ability library, and replacement effects.
  tags = cards, tcg, rules-engine, plugin, five-realms
  header
    mode = minimal

simpleGenFooter = {import:simple-gen-footer}


// =====================================================================
// DETERMINISTIC RNG
// =====================================================================
//
// A seeded xorshift32 PRNG. State is a plain integer so it lives directly in game state
// and survives JSON.stringify/parse -- no Math.random anywhere in this file.

frRngCreate(seed) =>
  let s = seed | 0;
  if(s === 0) s = 1;
  return s >>> 0;

frRngNext(state) =>
  let s = state >>> 0;
  s ^= s << 13; s >>>= 0;
  s ^= s >>> 17; s >>>= 0;
  s ^= s << 5; s >>>= 0;
  let value = s / 4294967296;
  return { value: value, state: s };

frShuffle(array, rngState) =>
  let a = array.slice();
  let state = rngState;
  for(let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
    let r = frRngNext(state);
    state = r.state;
    let j = Math.floor(r.value * (i + 1));
    let tmp = a[i];
    a[i] = a[j];
    a[j] = tmp;
  }
  return { array: a, state: state };


